Wait — but what about the bare `[rejected]` shape? Real git output: `! [rejected] HEAD -> branch (non-fast-forward)`. Covered by `[rejected]`. And git's other hint: `hint: Updates were rejected because the remote contains work that you do not have locally` (newer git, no "behind")? In that case there's still `! [rejected] ... (non-fast-forward)` in the output, so it's covered.

